+### 2.8 Raw Events and Park-on-Exit (host-driven native UI)
+
+These options exist so a host program can drive the glasses' native firmware UI through the gateway while the gateway keeps owning the BLE link.
+
+Raw inbound events:
+
+- `--raw-events` / `ble.raw_events: true` emits one `glasses.raw_packet` event for every notification on the `5402` command characteristic of either lens, before the gateway parses it. Frames the gateway consumes or acks itself (heartbeat echoes, page acks, touch events) are included. Notifications on the `7402` EvenFile characteristic (replies to `7401` writes made with `POST /api/raw {"char": "7401"}`) are emitted the same way with `"char": "7402"`; the gateway subscribes to `7402` on both lenses but never parses those frames.
+- `--raw-events-audio` / `ble.raw_events_audio: true` additionally emits raw packets for the `6402` microphone characteristic. This floods the WebSocket while the mic is on, so it is a separate switch and has no effect without `--raw-events`.
+- `--debug-raw-events` is kept as an alias of `--raw-events`.
+
+Park on exit:
+
+- Default (`display.park_on_exit: false`): when the glasses tear the gateway page down (`page_shutdown`: EvenHub cmd 9/10 or an ack with error code 9, typically after the user double-taps out of the app), the gateway immediately recreates its page and redisplays the cached content. `system.reinitialize {"reason": "page_shutdown"}` is emitted. This is the historical behaviour.
+- `--park-on-exit` / `display.park_on_exit: true`: on `page_shutdown` the gateway does **not** recreate the page. It leaves the native dashboard visible, sets `display_surface` to `dashboard`, sets `parked` to `true`, stops queued text traffic, and emits `system.reinitialize {"reason": "page_parked", "trigger": "page_shutdown"}`. Microphone requests made while parked are remembered and applied once the page exists again.
+- The page is recreated (full `createStartUpPageContainer`, then the cached display request, then the mic target) by any of:
+  1. the user launching the gateway's own dashboard menu entry (`Launch`). Two firmware paths are handled: (a) EvenHub cmd 17 with the gateway's menu app id: the gateway emits `glasses.dashboard {"action": "selected", ...}`, then `glasses.dashboard {"action": "launched", "app_id": ..., "via": "menu", "was_parked": true}`, then `system.reinitialize {"reason": "dashboard_launch", "app_id": ..., "via": "menu"}`; (b) firmware 2.3.2.14 sends no cmd 17 from a parked state and instead pushes app `0xE0` (EvenHub) to the foreground on SID `0x0D` (`{1: 1, 3: {1: 224}}`): the parked gateway treats that as the launch, immediately recreates the page and emits `glasses.dashboard {"action": "launched", "app_id": 224, "via": "foreground", "was_parked": true}` and `system.reinitialize {"reason": "dashboard_launch", "app_id": 224, "via": "foreground"}`. Because the firmware finds no page yet and reports OS event 7 (`system_exit`, and event 5 `foreground_exit`) within the same second, exit gestures arriving within 1.5 s of any launch are logged, still emitted as `glasses.touch`, but ignored for surface/page tracking; a `page_shutdown` (cmd 9/10) is not covered by that grace and still parks;
+  2. any `POST /api/display` (text, layout, image or clear): `system.reinitialize {"reason": "display_request"}` is emitted, then the page is created and the content rendered in that create;
+  3. `POST /api/page {"create": true}`: `system.reinitialize {"reason": "page_create", "was_parked": ...}`.
+- `--park-stops-heartbeat` / `display.park_stops_heartbeat: true` (default: follows `park_on_exit`, so it is on whenever `--park-on-exit` is on; `--no-park-stops-heartbeat` / `false` disables it): while parked the gateway stops sending the EvenHub heartbeat (SID `0xE0` cmd 12, every `heartbeat_interval_sec` to the right lens). The firmware's own dashboard only redraws pushed widget content (weather, calendar, ...) once the plugin heartbeat stops, so a host writing native widgets through `POST /api/raw` needs this. The heartbeat task keeps running (it just skips sends), so the background-task watchdog is untouched, the DevSettings heartbeat continues, and sending resumes within one interval after the page is recreated by any of the three paths above or by a reconnect. `/api/status` reports the effective value as `server.park_stops_heartbeat`.
+- `POST /api/page {"shutdown": true}` sends the EvenHub ShutDown (cmd 9) and parks the same way (`system.reinitialize {"reason": "page_parked", "trigger": "shutdown_request"}`). An explicit shutdown always parks, even when `park_on_exit` is false, so the gateway does not immediately undo it when the glasses confirm with cmd 9.
+- A BLE reconnect (full or right-lens) always runs the init sequence, which recreates the page; `parked` is reset to `false`.
+- `SYSTEM_EXIT` / `ABNORMAL_EXIT` / `FOREGROUND_EXIT` gestures keep their existing behaviour (surface marked `dashboard`, rebuild on next display call); only `page_shutdown` parks.
 
